  "summary": "Recent preprints give analytical treatment of localization, curvature-driven bias, and fluctuation-induced power laws in evolutionary and ecological models.",
  "synthesis": "Three preprints address how stochastic variation shapes equilibrium distributions in mutation-selection and ecological systems. The first derives a general Hill-number relation for quasispecies localization under Eigen's model, applicable to viral diversity measures. The second shows that fluctuating species interactions displace equilibria, yielding a universal power law with exponent 2 and critical noise scaling as N^-1 in ecological networks. The third finds that mutation-selection dynamics on degenerate fitness manifolds drift toward low-curvature, flat regions in a minimal evolutionary model. The dominant thread is fluctuation-driven redistribution of population or abundance across constrained states. The ecological and evolutionary results address distinct systems and are not unified by a shared derivation in these items.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-02-22"
